"""Digitized FCC groundwave field-strength-vs-distance curves.

Source: FCC 47 CFR 73.184 / 73.190 Graphs 1-20 (public domain U.S.
government work), downloaded from
https://www.fcc.gov/media/radio/am-groundwave-field-strength-graphs .
Each graph plots groundwave field strength vs. distance for a family of
ground conductivities, referenced to "100 mV/m unattenuated at 1 km";
this module keeps only the 3 mS/m curve (this app's single "average US
land" ground assumption - see am_groundwave.py) from each of the 20
frequency graphs, digitized directly from the PDFs' embedded vector
paths (not manually traced), and rescaled to a 1 kW reference using the
standard AM broadcast constant of 305.768 mV/m at 1 km per kW for a
quarter-wave monopole (so FCC's 100 mV/m at 1 km convention corresponds
to about 107 W here). Replaces a prior dependency on a third-party
Fortran package that carried an unresolved corporate copyright claim
with no accompanying license - see CLAUDE.md.
"""

